# Protocol-First Runtime Metrics Exposure

## Analysis

The server already has `MetricsTracker` with `turnsTotal`, `invalidOutputCount`, `actionAppliedCount`, `actionRejectedCount`, and `queuedActions`. The client HUD needs these values exposed via the protocol.

## Changes Required

### 1. Protocol: Add `runtime.metrics` Message Type

**File:** `packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`

Add a new message type to `ServerMessage` union and update the Zod schema:

```typescript
export type ServerMessage =
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "session.state";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "world.snapshot";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "agent.turn";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "agent.action";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "agent.feed";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "build.result";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "error";
      payload: { ... };
    }
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "runtime.metrics";
      payload: {
        turnsTotal: number;
        invalidOutputCount: number;
        actionAppliedCount: number;
        actionRejectedCount: number;
        queuedActions: number;
      };
    };
```

Add corresponding Zod schema entry in `clientMessageSchema` (for client-side validation if needed) or create a `serverMessageSchema` for runtime validation.

### 2. Runtime Server: Emit Metrics Snapshot

**File:** `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts`

Add a new helper method and call it periodically:

```typescript
private sendMetricsSnapshot(): void {
  this.emitMessage({
    version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
    type: "runtime.metrics",
    payload: {
      turnsTotal: this.metrics.metrics.turnsTotal,
      invalidOutputCount: this.metrics.metrics.invalidOutputCount,
      actionAppliedCount: this.metrics.metrics.actionAppliedCount,
      actionRejectedCount: this.metrics.metrics.actionRejectedCount,
      queuedActions: this.metrics.metrics.queuedActions
    }
  });
}
```

Call `sendMetricsSnapshot()` from the `tick()` method after queue depth is updated, and also in `sendSessionState()`.

### 3. Client HUD: Display Runtime Metrics

**File:** `apps/game-client/src/App.tsx`

Add state and HUD section:

```typescript
const [metrics, setMetrics] = useState({
  turnsTotal: 0,
  invalidOutputCount: 0,
  actionAppliedCount: 0,
  actionRejectedCount: 0,
  queuedActions: 0
});

// In message handler:
case "runtime.metrics":
  setMetrics(payload);
  return;

// Add new HUD card for metrics
<div className="hud-card">
  <button
    type="button"
    className="hud-card-toggle"
    onClick={() => toggleHudSection("metrics")}
    aria-expanded={!collapsedHudSections.metrics}
  >
    <span>Runtime Metrics</span>
    <span className="hud-card-toggle-icon">{collapsedHudSections.metrics ? "+" : "-"}</span>
  </button>
